      "textEn": "142\n\nThose who do not perform Brahmins are certainly despicable. Nowadays, human civilization is based on sensory gratification,\nTherefore, more and more people are becoming addicted to various things. No one respects the culture of Brahmins. The demonic civilization is attached to aggressive deeds, and for the satisfaction of deep desires,\nbig industries are established. As a result, the public suffers due to government taxes,\nPeople are irreligious, and they do not perform the yagyas (sacrifices) described in the Bhagavad Gita. Yagnyad bhavati.\nParjanyah—By performing Yagnya, clouds form and water rains, and due to abundant rain, great food is produced. If the state is run by Brahmins, then society should also follow the rules of the Bhagavad Gita. Only then,\npeople will be happy. When animals and humans eat plenty of food, they become strong,\nand their hearts and minds remain peaceful. Then they can live a spiritual life, which is the ultimate goal of life.\nDhruta Tanurushati, in the ancient\nThis is the essence, the supremely pure. Shamo damah satyamanugrahascha\n\nTapastitikshanubhavashcha yatra. 24). Meaning of the word\n\nDhruta—acquired through divine education; Tanu—body; Ushti—free from physical impurities; Me—mine; Purani—eternal; Yena—by which; Iha—in this world; Satvam—the quality of goodness; Paramam—supreme, the best; Pavitram—pure; Shamah—control of the mind; Dama—control of the senses; Satyam—truth; Anugraha—grace, kindness; Cha—and; Tapah—penance; Titiksha—endurance; Anubhava—\nKnowledge of God and the individual soul; Cha—and; Yatra—in which. The Vedas are the eternal divine Word, and, therefore, they are the Word of God. In this world, all Brahmins\nstudy the Vedas thoroughly and assimilate them, therefore they are considered\nthe direct embodiment of the Vedas. Brahmins are virtuous, as a result of which they possess the qualities of Shama, Dama, and Satya. They describe the original meaning of the Vedas, and by grace, 