ैश्वर्याणि",
      "textEn": "12\n\nTasya—his; H—undoubtedly; Yah—who; Purisha—of excrement; Surabhi—from fragrance; Saugandhya—becoming fragrant; Vayu—air;\nTam—that; Desham—country; Dasha Yojanam—up to ten yojanas (an eight-mile yojana); Samantat—around;\nSurabhim—fragrant; Chakar—did.Due to being in this state, the public did not bother Rishabhdev. But from their excrement,\nthe foul smell did not come out. On the contrary, their excrement was so fragrant that up to eighty miles\nthe region was filled with its fragrance. Meaning: From this description, we can imagine that Rishabhdev had divine bliss. Their excrement was completely different from the excrement of ordinary creatures; it was fragrant. In this physical world,\neven cow dung is considered sacred and deworming. How big a pile of dung is at one place.\nWhy not put it there, it won't smell bad. We can confidently assume that in Vaikuntha-Jagat, even excrement,\neven urine, is fragrant. In fact, the entire atmosphere became extremely fragrant from the excrement of Rishabhdev.\nAnd, having performed the duties of a cowherd, he sits and lies down, and drinks the milk from the cowherd's cow, and eats the leftovers. 34). Meaning of the word\n\nEvam—in this way; Go—cows; Mrig—deer; Kak—of crows; Charyaya—by action; Vrajan—wandering; Tishthan—\nStanding; Asinah—sitting; Shayanah—lying down; Kak-mrig-go-charitah—acting like crows, deer, and cows; Pibati—drinks; Khadati—eats; Avamehati—urinates; Smam—He did so. In this way, Rishabhdev followed the nature of cows, deer and crows. Sometimes they\nwalk here and there, sometimes they sit in one place. Sometimes, they also lay down. In this way, they behave like cows,\ndeer, and crows. They, like them, eat, drink, and excrete. Thus putting the people in a false sense. Meaning: Because of being God, Rishabhdev attained a divine body. Because ordinary people could not understand their\nnature and the practice of yoga, they started to bother them.\nTherefore, to deceive them,\nhe started behaving like a cow, deer, and crow. Thus, the one who follows the path of various yogas, the Lord, the lord of liberation, the supreme, the great, the blissful, the experience of all, in the self, of all.\nIn the self of all beings, the Lord, Vasudeva, of the self, without any fault, by the feeling of the next body, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete, the complete,"
