, and being able to see distant objects.\nAlthough they\nwere capable of doing all of this, but they did not use these powers. Reflective Question: Chaitanya Charitamrita (Canto 19.149)—\n\nA Krishna devotee—devout, selfless, hence peaceful. Bhukti-mukti-siddhim kaami—Sakala ‘Ashanta’. The word Shant means completely peaceful. Until all the desires of a human being are fulfilled,\nhe cannot be at peace. Every human wants to fulfill their aspirations and desires,\nwhether they are material or spiritual. The people living in the world are restless because their aspirations\nare countless. But a pure devotee is selfless. A devotee who is free from any desire for worldly pleasures,\nis free from all kinds of material desires. In contrast, all the workers are full of desires, because they\nwant to enjoy the pleasure of sensual gratification. They are neither at peace in this life, nor will they be in the next life. No"
