      "textEn": "1\n\nIt happened that all his yogic powers were lost. Even the supremely accomplished yogi can be ruined by the fickle nature of the mind.\nIt is possible. The mind is so fickle that it compels even a perfected yogi to be controlled by these senses. Therefore, to preach to all the yogis, Lord Rishabhdev performed the act of giving up his body.\nHe demonstrated it. While traveling through the Karnat, Konk, Venk, and Kutak regions in South India, they reached near Kutakachal. Suddenly, a fire broke out in the forest, in which that forest and Rishabhdev's body\nBecame ashes after burning. The king of Konk, Venk, and Kutak knew the pastimes of Rishabhdev as a liberated being. The name of this king was Arhat. Later, he became captivated by Maya, and in this situation,\nhe became the founder of Jainism. Rishabhdev established such religious rules that humans can be freed from material\nbondage. They ended all forms of atheistic activity.\nIn this earth, Bharatvarsh (India)\nA place (country) named (is) very sacred, because whenever God desired to descend, then\nHe descended in this land. Rishabhdev neglected all the yogic powers that the so-called yogis keep flaunting. Devotees are averse to the so-called yogic powers because of the grandeur of devotion. Yogeshwar.\nLord Krishna is going to demonstrate all the powers from his side to his devotee. More valuable than devotion, the power of yoga. Sometimes devotees are bewildered, and they begin to aspire for liberation and yogic powers. God is the one who fulfills all the desires of these devotees. Devotion is\nreceived only by those who do not desire liberation and yoga.\nRajovach\n\nNot, not, the divine self, the knowledge of the union of the self, the seeds of actions born of the knowledge, the gods, and the sufferings again.\nThey are born of chance. 1. Meaning of the word.\n\nKing said—King Parikshit asked; not—not; no—indeed; Bhagavah—Oh, all-powerful Shukadeva Goswami;\nAtmaramanam—devoted to devotion, of pure devotees; Yog-Samirit—obtained through yoga practice; Gyan—from knowledge; Avabharjit—burnt;\nKarmabijanam—of the seeds of karma; Aishwaryani—from the powers of yoga; Punah—again; Kleshadani—causing suffering; Bhavitum—to become;\nArhanti—are capable; Yadrichchaya—spontaneously, by themselves; Upagatani—are attained. King Parikshit asked Shukdev Goswami—Oh Lord, those who are completely pure in heart, them"
