      "textEn": "19\n\nIt is not controlled. According to the instructions of the scriptures, women should not be freed. When a woman and a girl\nlive, then the father should keep control over her. When she becomes a young woman, her husband\nAnd when she becomes old, her wise sons should control her. If she is given freedom,\nand is allowed to sit and stand freely with men, then she will go astray (corrupt). Such a corrupt\n(adulterous) woman, being swayed by adulterous men, can even kill her husband. Here,\nthis quote is presented so that the yogi who desires to be free from worldliness always\nkeeps his mind restrained. Srila Bhakti Siddhanta Saraswati Thakur used to say that upon waking up in the morning,\none should put on a hundred shoes on the mind, and before sleeping, one should beat the mind with a broom a hundred times. In this way, the human mind remains restrained. The condition of an uncontrolled mind and a woman who is adulterous is the same.\nIs.\nJust as an adulterous woman can kill her husband at any time, similarly,\none with an unrestrained mind, driven by lust, anger, greed, intoxication, envy, and delusion, kills a yogi. When a Yogi\nis driven by the mind, then he attains worldly status. A man should be mindful\nin the same way as a husband should be to his adulterous wife. Lust, anger, greed, delusion, fear, etc. Karmabandhashcha yanmoolah svikuryatkonu tadbudhah. Meaning of the word:\n\nWork: subject; anger: anger; pride: arrogance; greed: avarice; sorrow: remorse; delusion: delusion; fear: fear; beginning: all these;\nKarmic bondage: bondage for desire-driven actions; and; the root: the cause; will accept: will accept;\nWho: who; without doubt: without doubt; that: that mind; wise: if intelligent. The root cause of lust, anger, pride, greed, remorse, attachment and fear is the mind itself. All these\ntogether create the bond of karma.\nWho can trust a wise mind? Meaning: The mind is the root cause of physical bondage. There are many enemies 